Suggests: gnome-shell-extension-appindicator
Description: Thermal profile, battery charging and BIOS power settings
 Platform Power is a GTK4/libadwaita application and privileged D-Bus
 daemon that expose, on Dell laptops running Linux, the same category
 of settings Dell Command | Power Manager exposes on Windows: ACPI
 thermal/performance profile, battery charge-threshold management,
 and (on machines whose firmware supports it, via the dell-wmi-sysman
 kernel driver) BIOS-level extras such as Peak Shift, Advanced/
 scheduled battery charging and USB-C PowerShare.
 .
 It is an independent, original implementation built on top of
 standard Linux kernel interfaces and is not affiliated with or
 endorsed by Dell Technologies. Which advanced settings are available
 depends entirely on your machine's BIOS/firmware and kernel version.
